## WAKE TEST - #266 on the real sleeping database (read-only; only if slot 10 (e) reads RUN)
After PART P PASSED make NO SQL-touching request (no `/health/ready`, no signed-in page; the poller's `/health` and `/api/health` only, or none) and poll `az sql db show --query status` every 120 s (a control-plane read: it does not wake the database). When it reads `Paused` AND the activity log shows a `databases/pause` Succeeded row after your last SQL-touching request: one browser walk at 1440x900, Consultant: start page -> level -> landing -> **Engagements** (the click of `B991_STATUS.md:3`); time from the click to the rendered list; console errors; every response status the browser saw (BFF 504s to the browser expected 0); the error text of `describeFailure` absent; screenshots at the Loading state and the rendered state, opened and described. **Pass: the list renders within 100 s with 0 error text and 0 5xx seen by the browser.** If `Paused` is not seen within 45 minutes after your last SQL-touching request (someone else is using UAT), write `WAKE TEST: NOT RUN (the database did not pause: <times>)` and go on. A failed wake test on a healthy site: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` with the numbers (no rollback: the site is no worse than before), PART D not started. `CHECKPOINT WAKE TEST`.

